================================================================================
Complex rule builder: pre-save validate + rename gate, explain-on-open
================================================================================

Context:
In the Complex (SPARQL CONSTRUCT) rule editor, Save saved immediately — it did
not check that the query compiles, nor make the user review the agent-proposed
Name/Description. Opening an existing rule also did not reliably explain what
the current query does. Save is now a two-step gate (always validate, then ask
to review/rename before confirming), and the assistant explains an existing
rule up front.

Changes:
1. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-business-rules.js — Save flow reworked:
   - new _craValidate() (shared backend validation) and _craShowValidation();
     sparqlValidate() (manual button) now delegates to them.
   - sparqlSave() is a two-step gate: it always validates and informs in the
     chat; an invalid query is refused (error posted in chat); a valid query
     posts a success message and, on the first click, asks the user to review /
     rename the Name & Description and switches the button to "Confirm & Save";
     the second click performs the real save via the new _craDoSave().
   - _craSaveConfirmed / _craSetSaveConfirmUI / _craResetSaveConfirm manage the
     confirm state; it resets on modal open, on manual edits to
     name/description/query (input listeners), and when the agent rewrites the
     draft (_craApplyResponse).
2. src/agents/agent_complex_rule_builder/engine.py — SYSTEM_PROMPT "EDITING AN
   EXISTING RULE" now requires the assistant's FIRST message to explain, in
   plain language, what the current CONSTRUCT matches and infers before asking
   what to change (and never to ask the user to paste the query).
3. tests/units/agents/test_agent_complex_rule_builder.py — asserts the prompt
   explains an existing rule first (matches/infers, first message).
4. tests/units/front/test_business_rules_list_ui.py — contract tests for the
   two-step validate/confirm Save and the confirm-state reset.

Note: the SYSTEM_PROMPT change is a prompt change under CNS §3.5 — it adds to
the deferred eval debt already tracked for agent_complex_rule_builder.

Modified files:
- src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-business-rules.js
- src/agents/agent_complex_rule_builder/engine.py
